WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
This is part two of the five types:

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.240
the two where you find amounts.

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.200
K and a start, asking for the settled

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:08.520
concentrations.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.840
Or an old equilibrium, something added, and a

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:14.560
new value, asking how much was added.

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.040
They are the hardest two, so we take

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.640
them one step at a time.

00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:22.826
Type three: K and a start, and you

00:00:22.907 --> 00:00:24.986
want the settled concentrations.

00:00:25.307 --> 00:00:27.146
You can use the quadratic formula if you

00:00:27.307 --> 00:00:30.106
like, but HSC questions are written so you

00:00:30.187 --> 00:00:31.386
shouldn't need it.

00:00:31.467 --> 00:00:33.626
Look for a perfect square or a tiny

00:00:33.827 --> 00:00:34.666
K.

00:00:34.747 --> 00:00:36.906
N two O four splits into two N

00:00:36.987 --> 00:00:40.186
O two, K is 4.0 times ten to

00:00:40.227 --> 00:00:44.346
the minus four, and the start is 0.500

00:00:44.587 --> 00:00:46.906
moles per litre of N two O four,

00:00:46.987 --> 00:00:48.746
with no N O two.

00:00:48.827 --> 00:00:50.186
Which shortcut fits?

00:00:50.507 --> 00:00:51.786
Find the N O two.

00:00:52.267 --> 00:00:53.546
Pause here to answer.

00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:05.566
If x of the N two O four

00:01:05.647 --> 00:01:08.366
splits, the N two O four left is

00:01:08.447 --> 00:01:12.926
0.500 minus x and N O two is

00:01:13.007 --> 00:01:16.126
two x, so K is two x all

00:01:16.167 --> 00:01:20.206
squared, over 0.500 minus x.

00:01:20.527 --> 00:01:22.566
The bottom is not a square, so the

00:01:22.607 --> 00:01:24.326
square root will not help.

00:01:24.607 --> 00:01:26.846
But K is tiny next to the start,

00:01:26.927 --> 00:01:31.166
so drop the x: 0.500 minus x is

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:33.566
about 0.500.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:38.846
Four x squared over 0.500 is eight x

00:01:38.887 --> 00:01:42.366
squared, and that equals 4.0 times ten to

00:01:42.447 --> 00:01:43.886
the minus four.

00:01:44.007 --> 00:01:46.926
So x squared is 5.0 times ten to

00:01:46.967 --> 00:01:52.046
the minus five, and x is 0.0071.

00:01:52.087 --> 00:01:54.046
N O two is two x, which is

00:01:54.127 --> 00:01:56.286
0.014.

00:01:56.447 --> 00:01:59.006
Test it: the amount taken off the start,

00:01:59.087 --> 00:02:05.246
0.0071, is 1.4 per cent of 0.500,

00:02:05.367 --> 00:02:08.046
under about 5 per cent, so the shortcut

00:02:08.127 --> 00:02:08.766
holds.

00:02:09.967 --> 00:02:12.526
A huge K is the mirror image.

00:02:12.847 --> 00:02:17.566
Start with sulfur trioxide alone, 0.400 moles per

00:02:17.687 --> 00:02:20.766
litre, where K for sulfur dioxide and oxygen

00:02:20.847 --> 00:02:23.646
making it is 4.0 times ten to the

00:02:23.727 --> 00:02:24.046
ten.

00:02:24.607 --> 00:02:27.646
Almost nothing splits, so let the oxygen be

00:02:27.807 --> 00:02:28.206
x.

00:02:28.687 --> 00:02:31.886
Sulfur dioxide is two x, and sulfur trioxide

00:02:31.967 --> 00:02:34.446
is about 0.400.

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:41.666
In K, 0.400 squared is 0.160,

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:47.106
and 0.160 over four x cubed is 0.040

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.786
over x cubed.

00:02:48.907 --> 00:02:51.346
So x cubed is one times ten to

00:02:51.387 --> 00:02:54.546
the minus twelve, and x is one times

00:02:54.627 --> 00:02:55.906
ten to the minus four.

00:02:57.134 --> 00:03:00.013
Test it: the amount taken off the start,

00:03:00.094 --> 00:03:04.733
two x, is 0.00020, a

00:03:04.974 --> 00:03:08.413
tiny part of 0.400.

00:03:08.494 --> 00:03:09.773
Now the other way round.

00:03:10.014 --> 00:03:12.333
If you started with just the reactants, in

00:03:12.374 --> 00:03:14.653
the ratio of the equation, and K was

00:03:14.814 --> 00:03:17.213
huge, nearly all of it would turn to

00:03:17.414 --> 00:03:19.613
products first, and you would take a small

00:03:19.694 --> 00:03:21.293
x back from there.

00:03:21.374 --> 00:03:23.853
An excess of one reactant would stay.

00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:28.666
Type five is the hardest: an amount added.

00:03:28.987 --> 00:03:32.266
Carbon monoxide and steam make carbon dioxide and

00:03:32.347 --> 00:03:37.546
hydrogen, K is 4.00, and a 2.00 litre

00:03:37.627 --> 00:03:42.186
vessel holds, at equilibrium, 0.400 moles

00:03:42.227 --> 00:03:47.226
of carbon monoxide, 0.400 of steam and 0.800

00:03:47.307 --> 00:03:50.986
each of carbon dioxide and hydrogen.

00:03:51.307 --> 00:03:53.866
Steam is added, and the new equilibrium has

00:03:53.947 --> 00:03:57.426
0.200 moles of carbon monoxide.

00:03:57.707 --> 00:03:59.306
How much steam was added?

00:03:59.627 --> 00:04:04.266
First convert to moles per litre: 0.200,

00:04:04.347 --> 00:04:10.346
0.200, 0.400, 0.400.

00:04:10.387 --> 00:04:14.026
The new carbon monoxide is 0.100.

00:04:15.234 --> 00:04:17.793
Right after the steam goes in, before anything

00:04:17.874 --> 00:04:21.153
reacts, the vessel is the old equilibrium plus

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:22.753
the extra steam.

00:04:22.834 --> 00:04:25.313
So the unknown goes in the initial row:

00:04:25.394 --> 00:04:29.873
steam is the old 0.200 plus y, where

00:04:29.954 --> 00:04:32.033
y is the added steam in moles per

00:04:32.114 --> 00:04:33.153
litre.

00:04:33.194 --> 00:04:37.233
The new carbon monoxide, 0.100, goes in the

00:04:37.354 --> 00:04:40.993
equilibrium row first, so its change is 0.100

00:04:41.074 --> 00:04:45.793
minus the old 0.200, which is

00:04:45.994 --> 00:04:49.793
minus 0.100, and the ratio is one to

00:04:49.874 --> 00:04:51.393
one all round.

00:04:51.474 --> 00:04:55.313
Steam also falls 0.100, because some of the

00:04:55.434 --> 00:04:57.553
added steam is used up, and the two

00:04:57.634 --> 00:05:00.833
products each rise 0.100.

00:05:02.034 --> 00:05:06.753
At equilibrium that is 0.100, 0.100

00:05:06.874 --> 00:05:11.393
plus y, 0.500 and

00:05:11.514 --> 00:05:13.393
0.500.

00:05:13.714 --> 00:05:16.193
K has not changed, because the temperature has

00:05:16.314 --> 00:05:18.993
not: it is 4.00.

00:05:19.154 --> 00:05:24.113
So 0.500 times 0.500,

00:05:24.234 --> 00:05:28.913
all over 0.100 times the bracket 0.100

00:05:28.994 --> 00:05:33.633
plus y, equals 4.00.

00:05:33.674 --> 00:05:36.193
Solve for y, in moles per litre.

00:05:36.434 --> 00:05:37.873
Pause here and try it.

00:05:48.300 --> 00:05:54.160
The top is 0.250, so 0.100 plus

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:58.700
y is 0.250 divided by the product of

00:05:58.780 --> 00:06:05.340
4.00 and 0.100, which is 0.625,

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:09.620
and y is 0.525 moles per litre.

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:13.580
The vessel is 2.00 litres, so the steam

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:16.300
added is 1.05 moles.

00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:21.500
Check: 0.250 divided by the product of 0.100

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:27.180
and 0.625 is 4.00.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:31.100
The slips: 0.525 on its own forgets the

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.060
volume.

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:35.740
0.425 moles per litre forgets that some steam

00:06:35.820 --> 00:06:36.620
was used up.

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:39.673
So read what you are given and what

00:06:39.754 --> 00:06:40.553
you are asked.

00:06:41.034 --> 00:06:44.873
A start and a K, for concentrations: x,

00:06:44.954 --> 00:06:47.433
then a perfect square, or a tiny or

00:06:47.594 --> 00:06:50.233
huge K, and test any shortcut.

00:06:50.714 --> 00:06:53.753
An amount added: y in the initial row,

00:06:53.834 --> 00:06:56.233
K unchanged, answer in moles.

00:06:56.794 --> 00:06:59.833
Next: practice questions, each with a trap in

00:06:59.954 --> 00:07:00.233
it.

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:02.873
Here are the key notes.

00:07:03.114 --> 00:07:05.033
Pause the video if you need more time

00:07:05.114 --> 00:07:05.913
to copy them.
